HST Office: the HST version everywhere a user can see a version, in place of the engine's.

The engine version (26.8.x) stays internal (extension dependencies, help paths, first-start
detection, utl::ConfigManager::getProductVersion()). What users see now carries the HST
release from include/hst_version.h (scripts/write-hst-version.py):

- Document metadata: meta:generator (ODF) and docProps/app.xml Application (OOXML) are
  "HSTOffice/<HST release>$<OS>_<ARCH>", e.g. "HSTOffice/1.0.1$Linux_X86_64", without the
  engine version and the "LibreOffice_project/<build id>" part (was "HST_Office/26.8.1.1$...
  LibreOffice_project/..."). OOXML AppVersion stays "15.0000" (an Office compatibility value
  that other office suites parse). On import, xmloff maps "HSTOffice/1.0.x" to engine 26.8, so
  documents saved by HST Office keep the treatment of documents from that engine version.
- PDF: Producer "HST Office <HST release> (<arch>)" (was the engine version); Creator, which
  PDF readers show as the application, is "HST Writer", "HST Sheets", "HST Slides", "HST Draw",
  "HST Math" (was Writer, Calc, Impress, ...).
- EPS export: "%%Creator: HST Office <HST release>".
- HTML export generator and other "%PRODUCTVERSION%PRODUCTEXTENSION" texts: the HST release
  (was "1.0" followed by the engine's ".1.1", i.e. "HST Office 1.0.1.1").
- Insert > Object > OLE Object list, Writer AutoCaption object list and interaction message
  titles: %PRODUCTVERSION through the UI string hook (HST "1.0"), not the engine version.
- About: "Misc" reads "Sheets: tính đa luồng" (was "Calc: threaded"; Vietnamese like the
  rest of the dialog's introductory text, "Sheets: threaded" in "Copy version info"); "Copy
  version info" no longer has the "Engine:" line (Help > Báo lỗi still sends the engine
  version, labelled as such).
- Windows file description of the launchers: "HST Writer", "HST Sheets", "HST Slides",
  "HST Writer (Web)" (was "HST Office Writer", "HST Office Calc", "HST Office Impress").

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_xmloff_uxmloff (HST generators); tests/unit/test_hst_version_everywhere.py;
tests/runtime/check-hst-version-everywhere.py.
